+# Pinnacle³ — Replit → Vercel + Supabase Migration
+
+This document covers moving Pinnacle³ off Replit to **Vercel (all-in serverless)**
+with **Supabase Postgres**, and what still needs your hands-on setup.
+
+## What changed in the codebase (this branch)
+
+| Area | Before (Replit) | After (Vercel serverless) |
+|---|---|---|
+| API host | Long-running Express via `app.listen()` | Express app exported as a Vercel function — `api/index.ts` |
+| Startup seed | `seedReferenceData()` after `listen()` | `GET /api/cron/seed` (idempotent), run post-deploy |
+| Drive channel renewal | `setInterval` every 24h | Vercel Cron → `GET /api/cron/drive-channel-renewal` |
+| Pending-grants cleanup | `setInterval` every 6h | Vercel Cron → `GET /api/cron/pending-grants-cleanup` |
+| Cron auth | n/a (in-process) | `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` (Vercel injects it) |
+| Database | Replit Postgres | Supabase — pooled URL at runtime, direct URL for migrations |
+| Anthropic | Replit AI proxy (`AI_INTEGRATIONS_*`) | Direct `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (proxy still supported as fallback) |
+| Schema deploy | Replit Publish auto-migrate | `pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push` (you/CI run it) |
+| Frontend API base | relative `/api` | unchanged — SPA + API are same origin on Vercel |
+| Replit files | `.replit`, `replit.md` | removed |
+
+`index.ts` (the `app.listen()` entry) is kept for **local dev** (`pnpm --filter
+@workspace/api-server run dev`); Vercel never uses it.
+
+## 1. Supabase
+
+1. Create a project at supabase.com. Pick a region close to your Vercel region.
+2. Project Settings → Database → **Connection string**. You need both:
+   - **Transaction pooler** (port `6543`) → `DATABASE_URL` (runtime/serverless)
+   - **Direct connection** (port `5432`) → `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` (migrations)
+3. Push the schema from your machine (uses the direct URL automatically):
+   ```bash
+   DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://...:5432/postgres" \
+     pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push
+   ```
+4. **Data**: Supabase starts empty. Export your Replit Postgres
+   (`pg_dump`) and restore into Supabase, or migrate the tables you need.
+
+## 2. Vercel
+
+1. Import the GitHub repo `pinnaclecube/pinnaclecube` into Vercel.
+2. Framework preset: **Other**. Leave build settings to `vercel.json` (already
+   configured: pnpm install, build the `@workspace/pinnacle` SPA, output
+   `artifacts/pinnacle/dist/public`, and the `api/index.ts` function).
+3. Add all environment variables from `.env.example` (see below) under
+   Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
+4. **Plan note:** Vercel Cron and `maxDuration: 60` need the **Pro** plan.
+   On Hobby, crons run at most once/day and functions cap at 60s.
+
+## 3. Environment variables (Vercel)
+
+Set these (see `.env.example` for the canonical list):
+
+- `DATABASE_URL` — Supabase **pooled** (6543)
+- `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` — Supabase **direct** (5432)
+- `SESSION_SECRET`, `JWT_SECRET`, `JWT_EXPIRY`
+- `STAFF_SECRET`, `STAFF_SECRET_CHRIS`
+- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`
+- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`,
+  `STRIPE_EXCELLENCE_LAB_PRICE_ID`, `STRIPE_EVIDENCE_VAULT_PRICE_ID`
+- `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON`, `GOOGLE_DRIVE_ROOT_FOLDER_ID`
+- `GMAIL_USER`, `GMAIL_CLIENT_ID`, `GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN`
+  (and/or `RESEND_API_KEY`)
+- `CRON_SECRET` — random string; Vercel sends it as the cron bearer token
+- `CURRENT_DISCLAIMER_VERSION`
+- `NODE_ENV=production`
+
+## 4. Post-deploy: seed + webhooks
+
+1. **Seed reference data** (visa_criteria, orphaned-access fix):
+   ```bash
+   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" \
+     https://<your-domain>/api/cron/seed
+   ```
+2. **Stripe webhook**: point it at `https://<your-domain>/api/stripe/webhook`
+   and copy the new signing secret into `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. Raw-body
+   handling is already wired in `app.ts`.
+3. **Google Drive push channels**: existing channels point at the old Replit
+   URL. After deploy, re-register them at the new domain (re-run your
+   case-folder watch registration / the backfill endpoint), then confirm
+   `POST /api/drive/webhook` receives notifications.
+
+## 5. Known follow-ups / risks (not yet done)
+
+These need a live Vercel deploy to validate and may require one or two iterations:
+
+1. **`bcrypt` is a native module.** It often fails to load on Vercel's
+   serverless runtime. The fix is a drop-in swap to **`bcryptjs`** (pure JS,
+   hash-compatible — existing password hashes keep working) across the 5 import
+   sites (`services/auth.ts`, `routes/adminCases.ts`, `routes/adminInvoice.ts`,
+   `routes/adminSeed.ts`, `seed-demo.ts`). Deferred here because it changes
+   dependencies / the lockfile.
+2. **`pdfkit` fonts.** Generated PDFs need pdfkit's bundled `.afm` font data; the
+   serverless bundler may drop them. If PDF generation 500s, add the font files
+   via the function's `includeFiles`.
+3. **SSE (`/api/drive/events`, notification bells).** Serverless can't hold
+   long-lived streams. The client already polls in places; the clean fix is to
+   replace SSE with polling or **Supabase Realtime**. Until then, EventSource
+   will reconnect repeatedly without streaming.
+4. **The 5–10 min Drive backfill** (`POST /api/drive/backfill-subfolders`)
+   exceeds the function timeout. Move it to a queue (Inngest/QStash) or chunk it.
+5. **CI typecheck.** The repo has pre-existing type errors (loose `any`s in
+   several admin routes, a `p-retry` typing in the anthropic batch lib). A CI
+   gate should be added once those are triaged.
+
+## 6. Local development
+
+```bash
+pnpm install
+# API (uses index.ts + app.listen on PORT)
+PORT=3000 pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run dev
+# SPA
+pnpm --filter @workspace/pinnacle run dev
+```
+
+## 7. Verification checklist
+
+- [ ] `pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push` succeeds against Supabase
+- [ ] Vercel build green; SPA loads at the domain
+- [ ] `GET /api/healthz` returns `{ "status": "ok" }`
+- [ ] `GET /api/cron/seed` (with bearer) seeds `visa_criteria`
+- [ ] Login / register works (watch for bcrypt errors → item 5.1)
+- [ ] Stripe test webhook delivers and grants access
+- [ ] Drive webhook fires on a file change
+- [ ] Both Vercel Cron jobs show successful runs in the dashboard
